3. THE ORDERING SPACE (AAM-5)
==============================================================================
  15! = 1,307,674,368,000        log2 = 40.2501 bits   <- this record's order space
  21! = 51,090,942,171,709,440,000 log2 = 65.4697 bits   <- the brief's denominator
  12! = 479,001,600                                   <- already exhausted whole, section 2.1

  mechanism size                         k!     bits    of 15! orderings left of 15!   
  the brief: 3 boxes + 1 camera          24   4.5850    11.39% 54,486,432,000          
  measured: elements on the path        720   9.4919    23.58% 1,816,214,400           
  distinct objects on the path            6   2.5850     6.42% 217,945,728,000         
  distinct TEMPLATE words touched         2   1.0000     2.48% 653,837,184,000         

  the brief's own figures reproduce exactly under its own objects:
    4 points against 21!  ->  7.00% of the entropy, 2,128,789,257,154,560,000 orderings left
    which is the brief's 7% and its 2.1e18. The arithmetic is right;
    the objects are not this record's.

==============================================================================
4. WHAT THE PATH ACTUALLY TOUCHES (AAM-5)
==============================================================================
  element on the path              template word it belongs to
  face box A                       mask@4
  face box B                       mask@4
  face box C                       mask@4
  face box D                       mask@4
  `Order and stability` caption    order (gap pool, not the template)
  camera lens (1 of 2 cameras)     camera@2

  distinct template words touched: 2  ['camera', 'mask']
  the four boxes are four TOKENS of one word (`mask`@4 is a count of them),
  so their traversal order is the order of four copies of one word: no ordering.

  and the two words it does touch are ALREADY ordered by the template:
    camera@2 precedes mask@4.
  the path traversed A->camera gives mask before camera, which CONTRADICTS it;
  traversed camera->A it AGREES. yellow_polyline.md section 6: "The reading
  order (A -> camera) is a convention. The device has no arrowhead." -- so the
  one bit the mechanism could carry is unsigned, and either verdict is
  available by choosing a direction the measurement does not fix.

==============================================================================
5. THE 12-WORD SCOPE (AAO-1)
==============================================================================
  12! = 479,001,600          SWEPT WHOLE  (section 2.1: every rotation, both
                             directions, every reflection)
  15! = 1,307,674,368,000    ASSUMED      (section 2.13: twelve of fifteen slots)
  15! / 12! = 2730  (exact: 15 x 14 x 13)

  BUT THE 2730x IS A RATIO OF ORDERINGS, NOT OF WORK:
    the whole 12-word order space cost 359,251,200 derivations
      = 479,001,600 orderings / 16 checksum-valid x 12 passphrases
      and section 2.1 reports 359 million -- reconstructed exactly
    ONE ordering of the current template costs 1,363,720,121,280 candidates
      = 10,654,063,447 derivations (candidates/128, 21 words, floors)
    so one ordering of the fifteen is 29.66x the ENTIRE twelve-word sweep
    and the full 15! sweep is 1.783e+24 candidates -- the 5.5e9 GPU-years.
    (printed in scientific notation and never re-rendered as digits, per section 10)

